-- title:
--   Ld Gbcon Of Axis Self
-- statement:
--   **Slice evaluation is consistent with evaluation of vertical-line answers.** Let $S$ be a symmetric successor strategy, let $F$ be an indexed polynomial family, and let $\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta$ be errors. Assume the axis and self-consistency failures of $S$ are at most $\varepsilon$ and $\delta$, and assume $F$ is point-consistent with error $\zeta$. Let $\mathcal U$ be the uniform distribution on successor points, let $E_G$ be the family obtained by evaluating the slice at the successor point, and let $E_V$ be the family obtained from the vertical-line answer followed by point evaluation. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{ConsRel}_S\!\left(\mathcal U,E_G,E_V,
--   \zeta+\sqrt{8m\varepsilon+4\delta}\right).
--   $$
--
--   The proof combines point consistency with the point-to-vertical-line squared-distance estimate and a triangle inequality. This is the endpoint comparison used by the one-point sandwich estimates.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.ldGbcon_of_axis_self`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
